WEBVTT

00:02.002 --> 00:03.420
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:03.503 --> 00:05.495
You stole my kidney.

00:05.589 --> 00:08.957
You needed a father
and I needed a kidney. Get over it.

00:14.848 --> 00:16.600
I know you were raised in foster care,

00:16.683 --> 00:20.687
spent the four years prior to your
arrival on this island in a wheelchair,

00:20.770 --> 00:22.606
and I know how you ended up in it.

00:22.689 --> 00:28.612
What if I told you that somewhere
on this island there's a very large box,

00:28.695 --> 00:32.616
and whatever you imagined,
whatever you wanted to be in it,

00:32.699 --> 00:36.369
when you opened that box,
there it would be?

00:36.453 --> 00:40.499
I'd say I hope that box is big enough
to imagine yourself up a new submarine.

00:47.964 --> 00:49.956
You've really gone and done it now.

00:50.050 --> 00:53.094
You're not gonna start talking
about the magic box again?

00:53.178 --> 00:56.546
No, John. I'm gonna show you
what came out of it.

00:58.308 --> 01:00.383
Dad?

01:22.666 --> 01:24.376
Save your breath.

01:26.753 --> 01:30.173
Nobody's gonna hear you.

01:43.603 --> 01:44.636
Dad?

01:49.818 --> 01:52.571
- What is this?
- You tell me.

01:52.654 --> 01:55.407
- You brought him here.
- I didn't bring him here.

01:55.490 --> 01:58.118
I'd be careful about
getting too close to him.

01:58.201 --> 02:01.653
Where did you find him?
Why did you bring him here?

02:01.746 --> 02:03.988
I've already said, we didn't.

02:04.082 --> 02:06.835
- Want me to ask him how he got here?
- Be my guest.

02:09.379 --> 02:10.881
Tom.

02:12.299 --> 02:14.290
I warned you, John.

02:16.636 --> 02:21.600
Don't you know, John?
Don't you know where we are?

02:26.855 --> 02:30.942
- What did he mean?
- We don't have time to deal with that.

02:31.026 --> 02:33.320
We're leaving in the morning, all of us.

02:33.403 --> 02:36.490
Where are you going?

02:36.573 --> 02:39.493
We're going to a new place.

02:39.576 --> 02:44.487
Well, an old place, actually.
Would you like to come with us?

02:51.254 --> 02:53.413
- Yes.
- Good.

02:55.425 --> 02:58.345
We're holding Kate
a few buildings over from here.

02:58.428 --> 03:01.556
Maybe you'd like to say goodbye.

03:24.037 --> 03:26.790
Hey, where you going?

03:26.873 --> 03:29.032
I can't sleep if I'm not in my own tent.

03:29.126 --> 03:32.129
Fine. Let's go to your tent.

03:38.468 --> 03:43.849
It's nothing personal,
just old habits, you know?

03:46.685 --> 03:48.728
Fine. Scram.

03:50.272 --> 03:52.065
You want me to walk you home?

03:53.483 --> 03:56.027
It's five tents. I think I'll make it.

03:56.111 --> 03:58.905
You sure? I gotta pee anyway.

04:00.073 --> 04:02.451
That is so romantic.

04:23.930 --> 04:26.725
What the hell y'all doing?

04:27.767 --> 04:31.271
- What the hell are you doing?
- Going to take a leak.

04:33.064 --> 04:35.056
Yeah, well, so are we.

04:37.861 --> 04:40.186
Well, alrighty, then.

05:04.429 --> 05:05.931
Hello, James.

05:27.369 --> 05:28.703
Wanna zip your pants up?

05:31.081 --> 05:34.584
- What the hell are you doing here?
- Looking for you, actually.

05:35.794 --> 05:37.546
OK, Tarzan, so now you're back

05:37.629 --> 05:41.299
from your "Blow up everything
that can get us off the island" tour,

05:41.383 --> 05:43.426
tell me why you joined the enemy.

05:43.510 --> 05:46.638
I didn't join 'em. I infiltrated 'em.

05:46.721 --> 05:49.891
- You're undercover with the Others?
- That's right.

05:49.975 --> 05:53.426
How about you give me
one reason to believe that?

05:53.520 --> 05:57.649
Because a few hours ago, I snuck
into Ben's tent and kidnapped him.

05:59.734 --> 06:03.269
I tied him up,
dragged him off into the jungle.

06:03.363 --> 06:06.950
And you came all the way back here
to tell me this because...?

06:07.033 --> 06:12.497
Because this is the same man who
tortured you, beat you, humiliated you.

06:12.581 --> 06:16.115
And I want you to kill him.

06:20.839 --> 06:22.997
You want him dead, you kill him.

06:23.091 --> 06:25.416
- I'm not a murderer.
- Neither am I.

06:25.510 --> 06:28.180
Except for the man you killed in Sydney.

06:29.514 --> 06:33.560
They got files on us, James. All of us.

06:35.103 --> 06:37.397
Well, their files got their facts wrong.

06:44.196 --> 06:46.187
Then I made a mistake coming to you.

06:52.662 --> 06:55.457
Please don't tell anyone
that I was here.

06:55.540 --> 06:57.834
Hey, stop!

06:57.918 --> 07:00.410
I said stop!

07:02.589 --> 07:04.883
Damn it! Wait up.

07:19.981 --> 07:23.516
There. That ought to do it.

07:23.610 --> 07:28.187
Thanks. That would've taken me
hours to do myself.

07:28.281 --> 07:29.908
Glad I could help.

07:33.328 --> 07:36.832
Don't mind them.
They're all just excited you're here.

07:36.915 --> 07:40.669
- Excited?
- We've been waiting for you.

07:40.752 --> 07:43.672
John. You got a minute?

07:43.755 --> 07:46.299
- Yeah.
- Ben's asking for you.

07:47.425 --> 07:49.417
OK.

07:51.555 --> 07:55.058
<i>Ben</i>, <i>it's 6am on Saturday morning.</i>
<i>Kwon is pregnant.</i>

07:55.142 --> 07:58.895
<i>The foetus is healthy and was conceived</i>
<i>on island with her husband.</i>

07:58.979 --> 08:01.940
<i>He was sterile before they got here.</i>

08:02.023 --> 08:04.693
Hello, John. Thanks for coming.

08:05.735 --> 08:06.768
What's that?

08:06.862 --> 08:09.990
Juliet is gathering information
at your former camp.

08:10.073 --> 08:12.868
She's determining
if any of the women are pregnant.

08:12.951 --> 08:16.872
Then we're gonna go in and take them.

08:18.498 --> 08:19.749
Take them?

08:21.126 --> 08:25.213
This is not the first time we've done
this. Trust me, no one will get hurt.

08:27.382 --> 08:29.457
Could you pass me that, please?

08:33.472 --> 08:34.806
Thank you.

08:38.351 --> 08:41.146
I believe I have you
to thank for this, John.

08:41.229 --> 08:44.900
- Me?
- A week ago, I couldn't move my toes.

08:46.359 --> 08:51.948
But the minute you showed up,
I started to feel pins and needles.

08:52.032 --> 08:54.493
And this is only the beginning, John.

08:54.576 --> 08:57.245
I can't wait to show you
what this island can do.

08:58.246 --> 09:02.626
But, unfortunately,
you're not ready, John.

09:04.002 --> 09:06.463
- No, I'm ready.
- No, John, you're not.

09:07.672 --> 09:09.831
You're still crippled by the memories

09:09.925 --> 09:13.376
of the man you used to be
before you came to this island.

09:13.470 --> 09:17.766
You'll never be free until you release
the hold your father has over you.

09:20.143 --> 09:23.897
Why do you think you brought him here?

09:23.980 --> 09:25.889
The magic box.

09:25.982 --> 09:29.767
- OK, Ben, how about you show me the...
- Magic box is a metaphor, John.

09:29.861 --> 09:32.405
I can't show you anything
until you can show me

09:32.489 --> 09:34.324
that you're ready to be one of us.

09:34.407 --> 09:38.787
When people join us here on this island,
they need to make a gesture

09:38.870 --> 09:41.873
of free will, of commitment.

09:43.416 --> 09:46.461
That's why you're gonna
have to kill your father.

10:09.985 --> 10:11.820
Hey.

10:11.903 --> 10:14.614
- When did you get back?
- Jack, hey.

10:14.698 --> 10:18.201
Last night. Well, early this morning.

10:18.285 --> 10:23.196
So, camping, huh?
What were you guys doing out there?

10:24.458 --> 10:26.533
We figured we'd explore a bit,

10:26.626 --> 10:31.840
you know, see what was
further down the beach, male bonding.

10:31.923 --> 10:35.177
Well, next time you go out, sign me up.

10:35.260 --> 10:37.752
Yeah, next time, for sure.

10:49.107 --> 10:50.609
Thanks, Jin.

10:52.527 --> 10:55.812
- We have to tell Jack.
- Shouldn't he check out her wound?

10:55.906 --> 10:58.825
Can you give me your word
that Jack can be trusted,

10:58.909 --> 11:02.412
he spent ten days with those people
and nothing happened to him,

11:02.496 --> 11:04.654
- and that woman he's with...?
- Juliet?

11:04.748 --> 11:07.918
Aye, Juliet. Two weeks ago,
she had your friends in cages.

11:10.378 --> 11:13.381
Naomi. You heard everything
that she said.

11:14.508 --> 11:19.137
If we keep her safe,
she's our way off this island.

11:20.722 --> 11:25.685
So, given that,
do you trust Jack or don't you?

11:29.940 --> 11:34.767
Right. So we'd better bring in
someone we can trust.

11:44.246 --> 11:46.456
You should've put some shoes on.

11:46.540 --> 11:49.334
You think?

11:49.417 --> 11:52.254
So what else is in it?

11:52.337 --> 11:54.005
In what?

11:55.090 --> 11:57.081
The file they got on me.

11:58.135 --> 11:59.636
Not much.

12:00.470 --> 12:03.922
That your parents died
when you were very young.

12:04.015 --> 12:08.593
But it doesn't say
why your father shot your mother.

12:12.065 --> 12:14.192
Or why he turned the gun on himself.

12:20.198 --> 12:22.826
That must've been hard for you.

12:33.003 --> 12:36.006
- What else?
- High-school transcripts.

12:36.089 --> 12:40.802
Criminal record.
All the con jobs you were arrested for.

12:40.886 --> 12:43.211
I guess that's why
you use an alias, huh?

12:43.305 --> 12:45.547
Why did you choose the name Sawyer?

12:46.433 --> 12:50.103
How stupid do you think I am?
I already been conned by Ben once.

12:50.187 --> 12:52.981
Maybe you heard.
Bunny with a number painted on it?

12:53.064 --> 12:57.152
- You think I'm just gonna follow you?
- James, please. You have to trust me.

12:57.235 --> 12:59.988
Where are you taking me?
Tell me the truth.

13:00.071 --> 13:03.575
I'm bringing you there to do
exactly what I said, to kill Ben.

13:03.658 --> 13:05.650
- Why did you come to get me?
- I had to.

13:05.744 --> 13:08.288
- Why won't you do it yourself?
- James, please.

13:08.371 --> 13:11.958
Don't call me James.
Why won't you do it yourself?

13:12.042 --> 13:15.712
Because I can't! I can't! I can't do it!

13:19.299 --> 13:22.750
That's why I came back for you.

13:31.144 --> 13:32.646
Get up.

13:37.943 --> 13:42.113
I'll go to wherever you've got him, but
we're bringing him back to our camp.

13:42.197 --> 13:45.283
I ain't killin' nobody.
You understand me?

13:45.367 --> 13:48.453
Yeah, I understand.

13:50.080 --> 13:52.374
But you'll change your mind.

13:55.460 --> 13:58.912
When you hear what he has to say...

14:00.632 --> 14:02.467
...you'll change your mind.

14:20.819 --> 14:22.404
Hey, dude.

14:23.697 --> 14:25.157
Hello, Hurley.

14:35.667 --> 14:37.659
Can you keep a secret?

14:45.510 --> 14:49.890
- You've already spoken to her?
- Yeah, but you're gonna wanna hear it.

14:49.973 --> 14:53.591
- And you haven't told Jack?
- No.

14:53.685 --> 14:55.677
Good.

15:06.907 --> 15:11.286
My name's Sayid Jarrah. I understand
your helicopter crashed onto the island.

15:11.369 --> 15:13.497
Actually, it crashed in the water.

15:14.706 --> 15:18.157
- What's your name?
- Naomi. Naomi Dorrit.

15:18.251 --> 15:21.379
Naomi, from where exactly
did you take off?

15:21.463 --> 15:23.757
A ship, freighter.

15:23.840 --> 15:28.386
About 80 nautical miles west of here.
I'm part of a search-and-recovery team.

15:28.470 --> 15:32.474
You told my friends the wreckage
of Flight 815 was discovered.

15:32.557 --> 15:35.560
- Did you mean the partial wreckage?
- No.

15:35.644 --> 15:38.396
They found the entire plane
off the coast of Bali,

15:38.480 --> 15:41.024
in an ocean trench four miles deep.

15:41.107 --> 15:45.487
They sent down cameras in
these little robots to survey the wreck.

15:45.570 --> 15:47.447
The bodies were all there.

15:50.367 --> 15:53.036
Well, obviously we're not dead.

15:54.079 --> 15:55.194
Obviously.

15:55.288 --> 15:59.292
So, if you weren't looking for us,
then who were you looking for?

15:59.376 --> 16:00.710
Him.

16:02.504 --> 16:03.536
Desmond?

16:03.630 --> 16:06.800
My company was hired by
a woman named Penelope Widmore.

16:06.883 --> 16:10.971
I don't know why. I never met her.
She gave us a set of coordinates.

16:11.054 --> 16:14.724
We've been conducting a differential
GPS grid search ever since.

16:14.808 --> 16:17.050
You knew about the island?

16:17.144 --> 16:21.148
Island? We were given coordinates
in the middle of the bloody ocean.

16:21.231 --> 16:25.735
We thought it was a fool's errand,
until three days ago.

16:25.819 --> 16:30.198
I was flying back for the ship
when the clouds cleared and I saw land.

16:30.282 --> 16:32.273
The instruments started spinning.

16:32.367 --> 16:35.954
I realised I was going down,
so I grabbed my chute and I bailed.

16:40.208 --> 16:42.283
Did you actually see her helicopter?

16:44.087 --> 16:46.840
- No.
- You think I'm lying, mate?

16:46.923 --> 16:50.792
You have no means of communicating
with that freighter of yours?

16:52.971 --> 16:55.182
What was your name? Sayid?

16:55.265 --> 16:56.600
Yes.

17:06.902 --> 17:09.696
Remind me not to rescue you, Sayid.

17:36.848 --> 17:40.800
So, Ben. You said I'd kill him
when I heard what he's got to say.

17:40.894 --> 17:44.022
- That's right.
- Well, you wanna give me a heads-up?

17:44.105 --> 17:46.598
It's not really my place to tell you.

17:50.529 --> 17:53.813
Look, what you read in that file,

17:54.658 --> 17:56.733
about the guy in Sydney,

17:57.577 --> 17:59.371
I thought he was someone else.

17:59.454 --> 18:01.779
I made a mistake.
I didn't mean to kill him.

18:03.041 --> 18:05.116
Well, who'd you mean to kill?

18:13.927 --> 18:15.345
Are we almost there?

18:17.722 --> 18:19.766
Almost.

18:33.321 --> 18:35.699
Wake up, John.

18:36.908 --> 18:38.900
It's time.

19:09.316 --> 19:12.684
I know it won't be easy,
but the quicker the better.

19:16.907 --> 19:18.533
You're kidding me, right?

19:20.035 --> 19:22.954
You expect him to kill me?

19:25.499 --> 19:29.753
John, the hesitation that you're feeling
is just the part of you

19:29.836 --> 19:33.089
that still feels like he has
a perfectly good explanation

19:33.173 --> 19:37.302
for stealing your kidney, throwing you
out of an eight-storey window.

19:38.136 --> 19:41.014
Don't you wanna be free from him?

19:41.097 --> 19:44.434
The hesitation he's feeling
is because he is a spineless...

19:44.518 --> 19:46.353
Shut up!

19:53.777 --> 19:56.071
- I gotta think.
- Don't think, John.

19:56.154 --> 19:59.741
You're wasting your time, Bug-Eye.
We've been through all this.

19:59.825 --> 20:03.036
- All he wants is his daddy.
- Shut up! I said shut up!

20:07.165 --> 20:10.168
You really haven't figured it out yet,
have you?

20:12.587 --> 20:15.590
Let go of him, John.

20:17.259 --> 20:20.428
- Why are you doing this to me?
- Doing this to yourself.

20:20.512 --> 20:24.891
As long as he's still breathing,
you'll still be that same sad,

20:24.975 --> 20:28.395
pathetic little man
that was kicked off his walkabout tour

20:28.478 --> 20:31.273
because you couldn't walk.

20:55.088 --> 20:59.384
I'll be here the rest of the week, John,
if you change your mind.

21:15.192 --> 21:16.818
I'm sorry.

21:19.154 --> 21:21.281
He's not who we thought he was.

22:13.583 --> 22:15.168
Son of a...

22:25.345 --> 22:27.837
Nice place you got here, Locke.

22:29.891 --> 22:32.269
Ben's inside in the brig.

22:32.352 --> 22:34.344
You ready?

22:35.897 --> 22:37.889
Yeah, I'm ready.

22:58.170 --> 23:00.213
Friends of yours?

23:00.297 --> 23:03.831
It's an old slaving ship.
Mid 19th century.

23:10.682 --> 23:13.143
My guess is they captured the slaves,

23:13.226 --> 23:16.396
and brought them here
to try and mine the island.

23:19.774 --> 23:22.777
- What's in the boxes?
- That'd be dynamite.

23:28.116 --> 23:32.777
Son of a bitch.
You really kidnapped the little bastard.

23:37.334 --> 23:39.211
We ain't killing him, Locke.

23:40.670 --> 23:42.339
Whatever you say, James.

24:01.650 --> 24:03.641
Well, well, well.

24:06.029 --> 24:09.533
Hey! What are you doing?
Open the damn door!

24:09.616 --> 24:11.827
Shut up! Open up!

24:13.703 --> 24:15.945
I said shut up!

24:21.795 --> 24:24.256
Who the hell are you?

24:28.552 --> 24:31.555
- Is that like a radio?
- It's like a radio, yes.

24:31.638 --> 24:34.047
Never seen equipment
this sophisticated.

24:34.141 --> 24:37.425
- But you can still make it work, right?
- I hope so.

24:39.062 --> 24:41.054
And what about the other part?

24:41.148 --> 24:44.599
The part about they found the plane
and we're all dead.

24:44.693 --> 24:46.361
One thing at a time.

24:53.326 --> 24:55.454
There's not a single audible channel.

24:55.537 --> 24:57.528
Whatever that interference is,

24:57.622 --> 25:01.460
it's blocking our ability
to send our own transmission. If we...

25:01.543 --> 25:03.837
What's that? Is that a radio?

25:04.963 --> 25:08.091
- Where'd you get it?
- The luggage.

25:08.175 --> 25:10.583
What, you just found a radio
in the luggage?

25:10.677 --> 25:15.307
Kate, if I explain,
I want you to keep this very quiet.

25:16.349 --> 25:18.018
Keep what very quiet?

25:20.645 --> 25:25.275
Locke! Open this damn door! Open it up!

25:25.358 --> 25:27.517
I can hear you, you bald bastard!

25:32.741 --> 25:34.576
Rousseau.

25:35.285 --> 25:36.453
Locke.

25:38.705 --> 25:43.502
- What brings you to the Black Rock?
- Dynamite. And you?

25:43.585 --> 25:45.462
Open this door!

25:46.630 --> 25:48.757
Open up!

25:52.177 --> 25:54.502
Crates are right over there.

25:57.390 --> 26:01.061
- Open this damn door!
- Be careful. It's unstable.

26:07.275 --> 26:09.434
Locke! Locke!

26:21.998 --> 26:26.128
It's beautiful, isn't it? No matter
how much time you spend on the island,

26:26.211 --> 26:28.255
you just never get tired of this view.

26:28.338 --> 26:31.758
We haven't been formally introduced.
I'm Richard.

26:33.885 --> 26:37.055
- You mind if I join you here?
- Sure.

26:43.103 --> 26:46.690
- He wanted to embarrass you.
- I'm sorry?

26:46.773 --> 26:49.943
Ben knew you weren't gonna
kill your own father.

26:50.819 --> 26:53.446
He put you in front
of everyone in our camp

26:53.530 --> 26:56.199
just so they could all watch you fail.

26:56.867 --> 26:57.899
Why?

27:01.830 --> 27:05.876
When word got back here that there was
a man with a broken spine on the plane

27:05.959 --> 27:10.130
who could suddenly walk again, well,
people here began to get very excited,

27:10.213 --> 27:16.167
because that could only happen
to someone who was extremely special.

27:18.680 --> 27:21.933
But Ben doesn't want anyone
to think you're special, John.

27:22.017 --> 27:23.768
And why are you telling me this?

27:25.187 --> 27:30.984
Ben has been wasting our time
with novelties like fertility problems.

27:31.067 --> 27:33.278
We're looking for someone to remind us

27:33.361 --> 27:35.989
that we're here
for more important reasons.

27:37.949 --> 27:41.870
- What do you want from me?
- I want for you to find your purpose.

27:41.953 --> 27:45.874
And to do that,
your father has to go, John.

27:46.833 --> 27:48.825
And since you're not gonna do it...

27:55.383 --> 27:57.511
...l'm gonna suggest someone else.

28:02.349 --> 28:06.978
Sawyer? Why would Sawyer kill my father?
He doesn't even know him.

28:07.062 --> 28:08.563
Keep reading.

28:13.401 --> 28:17.270
Open this damn door! Son of a bitch!

28:26.706 --> 28:31.211
I'm pointing my gun at you, John Boy.
You got three seconds to open this door.

28:32.003 --> 28:34.162
You're not gonna shoot anyone, James.

28:35.340 --> 28:39.209
One! Two!

28:39.302 --> 28:43.640
If there were any bullets in that gun,
why would you hold a knife to my throat?

28:47.978 --> 28:52.482
- Son of a bitch!
- Guess I didn't raise no dummies.

28:52.566 --> 28:54.192
What the hell's that mean?

28:54.276 --> 28:58.029
It means that bald-headed bastard
outside the door is my son.

29:00.198 --> 29:05.162
- Come again?
- My son, as in, I'm his father.

29:05.245 --> 29:07.737
- You do speak English?
- You're his...

29:12.878 --> 29:16.923
- How did you get here, to the island?
- Island?

29:17.632 --> 29:21.251
OK. I'm driving down l-10
through Tallahassee,

29:21.344 --> 29:24.712
when, bam, somebody slams
into the back of my car.

29:26.850 --> 29:29.769
I go right into the divider
at 70 miles an hour.

29:29.853 --> 29:33.356
Next thing I know, the paramedics
are strapping me to a gurney,

29:33.440 --> 29:35.108
stuffing me in an ambulance,

29:35.192 --> 29:39.404
and one of them actually smiles at me
as he pops the I.V. in my arm.

29:39.488 --> 29:44.117
And then nothing, just black.

29:45.660 --> 29:49.664
And the next thing I know, I wake up in
a dark room, tied up, gag in my mouth.

29:49.748 --> 29:54.461
And when the door opens, I'm looking up
at the same man I threw out a window,

29:54.544 --> 29:57.120
John Locke,

29:57.214 --> 29:59.622
my dead son.

30:09.601 --> 30:11.728
Dead 'cause you threw him out a window?

30:11.812 --> 30:14.356
No, he survived that.

30:14.439 --> 30:18.109
But it paralyzed him, permanently.

30:18.193 --> 30:22.854
He's dead because the plane
he was flying on crashed in the Pacific.

30:25.659 --> 30:27.817
Well, I got bad news for you, Pops,

30:27.911 --> 30:31.081
'cause I was on that plane
with your son.

30:31.164 --> 30:33.156
He sure as hell wasn't crippled.

30:33.250 --> 30:36.837
We didn't crash in the Pacific.
We crashed here on this island.

30:36.920 --> 30:40.622
- You sure it's an island?
- Well, what else is it?

30:40.715 --> 30:43.635
Little hot for heaven, isn't it?

30:46.179 --> 30:48.473
OK. So we're dead?

30:48.557 --> 30:51.893
They found your plane
on the bottom of the ocean.

30:52.853 --> 30:56.940
One minute I'm in a car wreck, the next
I'm in a pirate ship in the jungle?

30:57.023 --> 31:02.237
If this isn't hell, friend,
then where are we?

31:07.993 --> 31:11.663
- Why did you throw Locke out a window?
- He was becoming a nuisance.

31:14.624 --> 31:17.200
I conned him into giving me
one of his kidneys.

31:17.294 --> 31:19.619
He never got over it.

31:21.131 --> 31:24.176
- Conned?
- Yes, sir.

31:24.259 --> 31:26.251
Conned.

31:32.559 --> 31:33.758
What's your name?

31:34.978 --> 31:40.139
- Your name.
- A con man goes by many names, friend.

31:40.233 --> 31:43.069
I've been Alan Seward, Anthony Cooper,

31:43.153 --> 31:47.324
Ted MacLaren, Tom Sawyer,
Louis Jackson, Paul...

31:47.407 --> 31:49.701
Tom Sawyer?

31:49.785 --> 31:52.454
I was young and Huck Finn was taken.

31:53.121 --> 31:57.167
And the ladies loved that one.
Made me charming.

32:02.088 --> 32:04.466
Well, how about that?

32:05.884 --> 32:07.552
How about what?

32:10.347 --> 32:12.338
Sawyer's my name, too.

32:36.164 --> 32:39.000
Ben, what's going on?

32:39.084 --> 32:41.628
- We're moving.
- Moving? Where are we going?

32:41.711 --> 32:45.882
"We" are not going anywhere, John.
You are going to stay behind.

32:45.966 --> 32:48.458
You both are going to stay behind.

32:48.552 --> 32:51.263
What? You're not taking him?

32:51.346 --> 32:53.890
He's your mess, John.
Why would we clean it up?

32:53.974 --> 32:56.466
Ben, if you're trying to embarrass me...

32:56.560 --> 32:59.354
Where would you get
a ridiculous idea like that?

33:00.188 --> 33:02.513
You can't leave me. After everything...

33:02.607 --> 33:05.277
Don't tell me what I can't do, John.

33:08.530 --> 33:11.324
But I thought I was special.

33:13.827 --> 33:16.288
Well, everyone makes mistakes.

33:19.541 --> 33:23.326
We're leaving now.
We'll leave a trail, one you can track.

33:23.420 --> 33:24.671
And, John...

33:25.797 --> 33:28.967
unless you're carrying
your father's body on your back,

33:30.051 --> 33:31.720
don't bother.

34:04.461 --> 34:06.619
What's the matter with you?

34:07.798 --> 34:10.342
You ever been to Jasper, Alabama?

34:12.177 --> 34:13.459
Why?

34:13.553 --> 34:16.181
Have you or haven't you?

34:17.307 --> 34:19.351
Yeah, I've been to Jasper.

34:19.935 --> 34:22.562
Don't tell me I'm your daddy.

34:23.438 --> 34:28.266
No. You killed my daddy.

34:49.339 --> 34:50.882
Read it.

34:57.764 --> 34:59.756
"Dear Mr Sawyer..."

35:02.310 --> 35:04.938
- What is this?
- Just read it.

35:07.774 --> 35:10.183
"You don't know who I am,

35:10.277 --> 35:15.240
but I know who you are,
and I know what you done."

35:15.323 --> 35:18.410
"You had sex with my mother

35:18.493 --> 35:22.164
and then you stole
my dad's money all away,

35:22.247 --> 35:26.960
so he got angry and he killed my mother

35:27.043 --> 35:30.797
and then he killed himself."

35:30.881 --> 35:32.382
Blah, blah, blah, blah.

35:34.468 --> 35:39.598
So, what, is this supposed to be you?
You wrote this letter?

35:41.057 --> 35:42.309
Hey, wait a second.

35:43.310 --> 35:47.147
Did you take my name because you were
on some kind of revenge kick?

35:49.274 --> 35:52.068
- Keep reading.
- Easy, easy.

35:52.152 --> 35:54.446
Don't get all worked up.

35:54.529 --> 36:00.202
Look, I ran that con two dozen times.
If your mother was one of the ladies...

36:00.285 --> 36:01.912
Mary.

36:03.789 --> 36:05.780
Her name was Mary.

36:08.752 --> 36:12.287
Mary from Jasper, Alabama.

36:12.380 --> 36:15.050
Yeah, I remember her.

36:16.134 --> 36:19.888
She practically begged me
to take her $38,000

36:19.971 --> 36:22.891
and to rescue her
from her sorry little life.

36:24.935 --> 36:28.688
- Finish the letter.
- Look, I only took her money.

36:28.772 --> 36:31.014
It ain't my fault your dad overreacted.

36:31.107 --> 36:35.362
If he pulled the old murder<i>l</i>suicide,
then I'm sure he's down here somewhere.

36:35.445 --> 36:37.489
Maybe you could take this up with him.

36:37.572 --> 36:39.407
- Finish it!

36:42.119 --> 36:43.151
OK.

36:44.955 --> 36:46.665
OK.

36:57.217 --> 37:00.720
You wanna go to hell?
You wanna go to hell?

37:50.770 --> 37:52.439
Thank you.

37:59.779 --> 38:03.617
- You missing those cheeseburgers yet?
- Only every second.

38:06.369 --> 38:07.954
- Hey.
- Hey.

38:08.038 --> 38:09.623
I need to talk to you.

38:11.124 --> 38:12.156
OK.

38:12.250 --> 38:14.461
- In private.
- No problem.

38:14.544 --> 38:16.953
Anything you wanna say,
say in front of her.

38:17.047 --> 38:19.174
- Not this.
- It's OK.

38:19.257 --> 38:21.666
No, no, no, no. You can stay.

38:23.261 --> 38:27.390
Yeah, you should stay. Seems only fair,
considering that she's the reason

38:27.474 --> 38:30.560
no one wants to tell you
there's a woman in Hurley's tent

38:30.644 --> 38:33.052
who parachuted
onto the island yesterday.

38:33.146 --> 38:35.690
- What?
- A woman jumped from her chopper.

38:35.774 --> 38:39.110
She says the boat she took off from
is 80 miles off the coast

38:39.194 --> 38:42.614
and if she can find a way
to contact it, we'll all be rescued.

38:42.697 --> 38:44.908
Why didn't anyone tell me this?

38:46.284 --> 38:49.621
Nobody told you
because they don't trust you.

38:57.712 --> 39:00.423
- How?
- How what?

39:00.507 --> 39:03.635
- How does she contact her boat?
- Did you hear what I said?

39:03.718 --> 39:06.346
Hurley, Charlie,
your friends, are afraid...

39:06.429 --> 39:08.974
Kate! How?

39:14.020 --> 39:18.900
She had a phone-radio thing.
Sayid's trying to get it to work.

39:22.237 --> 39:23.697
We should tell her.

39:26.533 --> 39:28.524
- No.
- Tell me what?

39:28.618 --> 39:31.413
- We should tell her.
- Not yet.

39:56.396 --> 39:58.388
You can go back now.

40:00.066 --> 40:01.693
Why did you do this?

40:03.737 --> 40:07.605
He ruined my life. And he ruined yours.

40:11.244 --> 40:12.996
And he had it coming.

40:17.459 --> 40:20.212
- Juliet is a mole.
- What?

40:20.295 --> 40:24.591
She's working for Ben. He sent her back
to find out which women were pregnant.

40:24.674 --> 40:28.595
Three days from now there's gonna be
a raid, and they're gonna take them.

40:28.678 --> 40:31.056
They say they don't want anyone
to get hurt.

40:32.682 --> 40:35.727
- Why are you telling me this?
- So you can warn the camp.

40:35.811 --> 40:37.270
You warn the camp.

40:38.897 --> 40:40.232
I'm not going back.

40:40.982 --> 40:42.776
You're going back undercover?

40:44.361 --> 40:47.531
No, I was never undercover, James.

40:47.614 --> 40:49.991
I'm on my own journey now.

40:51.701 --> 40:54.621
Even if Juliet is a mole,
they ain't gonna believe me.

40:54.704 --> 40:57.030
I've been saying that
since she showed up.

40:58.917 --> 41:00.377
They'll believe you now.

41:05.590 --> 41:06.925
Hey.

41:08.927 --> 41:10.762
Is it true?

41:11.847 --> 41:15.517
- Is what true?
- That he threw you out a window.

41:18.478 --> 41:21.439
That you were a cripple.

41:23.942 --> 41:25.527
Not anymore.
